1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
You

2
00:00:22,300 --> 00:00:26,620
Whoa, that's weird. I'm shaking

3
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:44,120
But I felt fine ever since becoming a zombie

4
00:00:44,120 --> 00:00:47,380
Is there something wrong with me?

5
00:00:47,380 --> 00:00:51,380
I have to tell Mr. Kotaro

6
00:00:51,380 --> 00:01:15,220
So looks like we're lost at sea

7
00:01:15,220 --> 00:01:17,420
Well, this is surprising

8
00:01:17,420 --> 00:01:20,560
But which way are we going? Can we get back?

9
00:01:20,560 --> 00:01:23,340
Take it easy. Zombies can't drown, probably

10
00:01:23,340 --> 00:01:26,700
Then let's find an island! We can start all over

11
00:01:26,700 --> 00:01:30,320
Zombie survival, huh? Sounds like fun. Count me in

12
00:01:30,320 --> 00:01:35,980
For starters, we might want to do our makeup in case anything happens

13
00:01:35,980 --> 00:01:38,980
This is a disaster

14
00:01:38,980 --> 00:01:51,260
Damn it, my phone's not working

15
00:01:51,260 --> 00:01:56,260
It's just like the depopulation

16
00:01:56,260 --> 00:01:59,420
The curse that comes with the Reiwa era

17
00:01:59,420 --> 00:02:05,220
A year ago, if we'd fixed it while we were still in Heisei instead

18
00:02:05,220 --> 00:02:07,420
This tragedy could have been stopped

19
00:02:07,420 --> 00:02:10,420
We need to get out of here immediately

20
00:02:10,420 --> 00:02:28,700
Oh, we just ended up back in Saga

21
00:02:28,700 --> 00:02:31,300
And not far from where we started

22
00:02:31,300 --> 00:02:34,540
Come on, I know it's a small place but still

23
00:02:34,540 --> 00:02:36,320
What's in there, Lady Junko?

24
00:02:36,580 --> 00:02:38,940
Oh, those are my tools for making Ozaki dolls.

25
00:02:39,340 --> 00:02:40,940
I was afraid they would get wet.

26
00:02:41,340 --> 00:02:43,400
You're ever the diligent worker, I see.

27
00:02:45,100 --> 00:02:46,220
Hey, what's wrong?

28
00:02:52,040 --> 00:02:53,960
It's about to bite the duck!

29
00:02:53,980 --> 00:02:56,820
Uh-oh. We better go get our crap out. Quick!

30
00:03:04,540 --> 00:03:25,360
Looks like our house is gone, and everything we own.

31
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:29,680
Our costumes, and Mr. Kotaro's instruments as well.

32
00:03:29,980 --> 00:03:31,800
Wait, oh no! Our makeup too!

33
00:03:31,920 --> 00:03:32,640
That's bad!

34
00:03:32,640 --> 00:03:35,840
I'm so sorry, guys. I should have grabbed that, not my tools.

35
00:03:36,920 --> 00:03:40,440
Well then, things have taken a clear turn for the worse.

36
00:03:40,960 --> 00:03:43,980
If we keep turning toward the worst, maybe we'll do a donut?

37
00:03:45,140 --> 00:03:46,540
I sure hope so.

38
00:03:46,900 --> 00:03:49,520
More importantly, what are we going to do now?

39
00:03:51,200 --> 00:03:51,680
Sanko?

40
00:03:53,160 --> 00:03:53,640
Machiko!

41
00:03:53,640 --> 00:03:56,120
What are you girls doing out here on the beach?

42
00:03:56,220 --> 00:03:56,640
Hishi!

43
00:03:57,000 --> 00:03:58,760
Oh, she works with me at the factory.

44
00:03:59,720 --> 00:04:02,120
I guess our house got washed away.

45
00:04:02,120 --> 00:04:04,240
That big pile of debris was your house?

46
00:04:04,360 --> 00:04:06,160
My goodness, you poor children.

47
00:04:06,680 --> 00:04:08,180
Do you have no place to go?

48
00:04:08,400 --> 00:04:09,740
You should come down to Kation.

49
00:04:10,080 --> 00:04:11,460
It's been turned into a shelter.

50
00:04:16,740 --> 00:04:17,500
Oh, man.

51
00:04:17,740 --> 00:04:20,160
The damage must be much worse than we imagined.

52
00:04:20,160 --> 00:04:24,280
The actual shelter was too much of a mess to stay in, so we're here.

53
00:04:24,680 --> 00:04:26,060
It'll have to do for now.

54
00:04:27,060 --> 00:04:29,460
In times like this, people always tell you,

55
00:04:29,540 --> 00:04:31,720
try to put on a brave face.

56
00:04:32,160 --> 00:04:33,940
But it's hard, you know?

57
00:04:34,660 --> 00:04:37,060
I wonder if Mr. Kotaro is okay.

58
00:04:40,360 --> 00:04:40,800
Sorry.

59
00:04:40,800 --> 00:04:43,600
This is the only space we have for you girls.

60
00:04:43,680 --> 00:04:44,580
Don't be sorry.

61
00:04:44,940 --> 00:04:46,000
We're just relieved.

62
00:04:46,260 --> 00:04:48,400
We're happy you let us borrow the tarp as well.

63
00:04:48,780 --> 00:04:49,560
Thanks a lot.

64
00:04:49,760 --> 00:04:50,760
Yeah, you're the best.

65
00:04:50,860 --> 00:04:51,520
Thank you!

66
00:04:52,040 --> 00:04:54,520
I figure it'll be helpful since you're so popular.

67
00:04:55,360 --> 00:04:57,700
There's cardboard to sit on and blankets downstairs.

68
00:04:58,160 --> 00:04:59,060
Come grab some later.

69
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:00,200
Oh!

70
00:05:00,260 --> 00:05:02,340
And would you mind introducing everyone, Sanko?

71
00:05:03,060 --> 00:05:04,720
Uh, my name is...

72
00:05:04,720 --> 00:05:05,440
That's Ichiko.

73
00:05:05,580 --> 00:05:06,380
I'm Niko.

74
00:05:06,660 --> 00:05:09,260
And that's Yonko, Itsuko, and Matsuko.

75
00:05:10,140 --> 00:05:11,780
Oh, numerical names.

76
00:05:12,120 --> 00:05:13,060
I'm Machiko.

77
00:05:13,540 --> 00:05:14,840
Wait, where's that...

78
00:05:14,840 --> 00:05:15,480
Zero-ko?

79
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:17,260
I don't see her.

80
00:05:20,860 --> 00:05:22,460
Here you go, man.

81
00:05:23,820 --> 00:05:26,140
You probably shouldn't eat that, Zero-ko!

82
00:05:27,240 --> 00:05:28,800
We're sorry about her.

83
00:05:29,160 --> 00:05:30,460
Nothing to worry about.

84
00:05:30,460 --> 00:05:32,380
I know you girls have been through a lot.

85
00:05:32,700 --> 00:05:33,900
You must be hungry.

86
00:05:34,420 --> 00:05:35,020
Go ahead.

87
00:05:38,520 --> 00:05:41,340
My, you're even hungrier than I thought, aren't you?

88
00:05:41,960 --> 00:05:42,320
Hi!

89
00:05:42,540 --> 00:05:44,080
Can we help you guys with anything?

90
00:05:44,620 --> 00:05:47,100
Yes, we could definitely use a few extra hands.

91
00:05:47,100 --> 00:06:13,580
Everyone at the factory knows you're a hard worker, Sanko.

92
00:06:13,580 --> 00:06:15,480
And I guess that goes for your friends, too.

93
00:06:15,900 --> 00:06:17,320
But don't wear yourselves out.

94
00:06:17,440 --> 00:06:20,080
The rest of us will be in real trouble without your help.

95
00:06:20,660 --> 00:06:22,220
Oh, you don't have to worry about us.

96
00:06:22,300 --> 00:06:23,240
We're actually dead.

97
00:06:23,620 --> 00:06:23,960
Dead!

98
00:06:24,200 --> 00:06:24,860
Set on working!

99
00:06:24,860 --> 00:06:25,120
Huh?

100
00:06:26,580 --> 00:06:27,500
Oh, rest, rest.

101
00:06:27,580 --> 00:06:29,240
I want to go home now!

102
00:06:29,760 --> 00:06:30,080
Huh?

103
00:06:30,680 --> 00:06:32,220
Please, can we leave?

104
00:06:32,320 --> 00:06:33,180
I'm scared.

105
00:06:33,920 --> 00:06:34,400
Yeah.

106
00:06:34,960 --> 00:06:36,820
Please, can we go home?

107
00:06:36,820 --> 00:06:52,940
One, two, three, four!

108
00:06:52,940 --> 00:07:17,380
Oh, rest, rest.

109
00:07:17,380 --> 00:07:39,380
Okuba!

110
00:07:39,380 --> 00:07:40,380
Hm?

111
00:07:40,380 --> 00:07:42,380
I have an idea of what's happening!

112
00:07:42,380 --> 00:07:43,380
How about is it?

113
00:07:43,380 --> 00:07:45,380
Well, it's all of Saga.

114
00:07:45,380 --> 00:07:47,380
And some neighboring prefectures too.

115
00:07:47,380 --> 00:07:51,380
A bunch of towers are knocked over, so it's not just power, it's internet and phones.

116
00:07:51,380 --> 00:07:52,380
That's just great.

117
00:07:52,380 --> 00:07:55,380
This is why I said we needed a satellite phone for work.

118
00:07:55,380 --> 00:07:57,380
And the roads are a total mess as well.

119
00:07:57,380 --> 00:08:02,380
Apparently in the areas that were hit the hardest, they've got people staying in shelters now.

120
00:08:02,380 --> 00:08:05,380
So, should we split up again?

121
00:08:09,380 --> 00:08:13,380
At Kation in Kuratsu, many citizens are taking shelter.

122
00:08:13,380 --> 00:08:15,380
I'm with NBK Fukuoka.

123
00:08:15,380 --> 00:08:17,380
How would you describe things here, sir?

124
00:08:17,380 --> 00:08:19,380
I gotta tell ya, it's been absolutely wild!

125
00:08:19,380 --> 00:08:20,380
Just look around!

126
00:08:20,380 --> 00:08:24,380
You're looking at the biggest shelter in the area, so all of Saga is here!

127
00:08:24,380 --> 00:08:26,380
I mean, not all of Saga.

128
00:08:26,380 --> 00:08:29,380
But it does feel kinda weird sleeping where you used to shop!

129
00:08:29,380 --> 00:08:33,380
For one thing, I'm going to miss my house.

130
00:08:33,380 --> 00:08:37,380
But still, everybody here is trying their best to stay positive.

131
00:08:37,380 --> 00:08:41,380
If it weren't for that, I probably would've broken down crying by now.

132
00:08:41,380 --> 00:08:45,380
In fact, I know I would've, so I'm grateful to be here.

133
00:08:45,380 --> 00:08:50,380
Well, we're more concerned about kids and the elderly, and we might be here for a while.

134
00:08:50,380 --> 00:08:52,380
We actually have a few kids of our own.

135
00:08:52,380 --> 00:08:56,380
The youngest is two years old, and you wouldn't believe how much that kiddo takes after her mother.

136
00:08:56,380 --> 00:08:57,380
It's really a sight to see.

137
00:08:57,380 --> 00:09:00,380
Luckily, those nice girls are always around to keep them occupied.

138
00:09:00,380 --> 00:09:01,380
Oh, hey!

139
00:09:01,380 --> 00:09:02,380
